WEB SOURCE (the specification — read end to end)
  web/src/features/vehicles/pages/VehicleAccessPage.tsx  (route /vehicles/:id/access)
    <PageContainer title="Vehicle Access" subtitle="Manage drivers and share invitations"
                   loading={driversLoading || invitationsLoading}> hosting two <GlassPanel> sections:
    GlassPanel1 — Drivers (Users icon + "Drivers" + count Badge + ghost "Refresh"[aria drivers.refresh]):
      drivers.length > 0 ? <DataTable cols=[name, email, role(Badge info | —), remove(per-row ghost
      UserMinus, shown iff row.share_user_id != null)]> : <EmptyState Users "drivers.empty">.
    GlassPanel2 — Share Invitations (Mail icon + "Share Invitations" + count + ghost "Refresh"
      [aria invitations.refresh] + primary "Invite Driver"[aria invitations.create]):
      invitations.length > 0 ? <DataTable cols=[status(<StatusBadge> pending→online/revoked→offline/
      else→asleep), createdBy, expires(<TimeStamp>), link(<CopyButton> iff invite_url),
      revoke(per-row ghost XCircle, shown iff status==='pending')]> : <EmptyState Shield
      "invitations.empty">.
    Two <ConfirmDialog variant="danger">: removeTarget (drivers.removeTitle/Message/Confirm) and
      revokeTarget (invitations.revokeTitle/Message/Confirm).
  Hooks (8): useVehicle, useVehicleDrivers (GET /vehicles/{id}/drivers), useVehicleInvitations
    (GET /vehicles/{id}/invitations), useRefreshVehicleDrivers (POST …/drivers/refresh),
    useRefreshVehicleInvitations (POST …/invitations/refresh), useRemoveVehicleDriver
    (DELETE …/drivers {share_user_id}), useCreateVehicleInvitation (POST …/invitations),
    useRevokeVehicleInvitation (POST …/invitations/{invitationId}/revoke). Each mutation invalidates
    its list query on success. Hook names ported verbatim to the Swift seam call sites.
  Types: VehicleDriver{id, share_user_id?, driver_email?, driver_name?, role?} ·
    VehicleInvitation{id, invitation_id, invite_url?, status, expires_at?, created_by?, created_at}.
  i18n: 27 keys under the en.json `vehicleAccess` group — captured verbatim (the canonical en.json
    values, e.g. drivers.empty="No drivers found", invitations.empty="No invitations found").

PATH / CONVENTION ADAPTATION  (no silent drift — disclosed in full)
  The generated prompt names the output `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Vehicles/VehicleAccessPage.swift`
  and gates `swiftlint/check-placeholders` on `…/Features/Vehicles`. That path is an IDEALISED
  generator default — it exists in NO part of this repo's reality:
    • project.yml builds `Sources`, `TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets`, `TeslaSync/feature-views`,
      `Localization`, `../design/generated/apple` — NOT `TeslaSync/Features/**`.
    • .swiftlint.yml `included:` lists `TeslaSync/feature-views` — NOT `TeslaSync/Features/**`.
    • Every one of the 1436 existing surface files + every recent P4 commit (LiveControls, AiUsageCard,
      helpers, AnomalyInlineRow, FSMStateDiagram, …) ships under `TeslaSync/feature-views/<Stem>.*`.
  Writing to `Features/Vehicles` would compile + lint NOTHING (not in project.yml / swiftlint roots),
  making the build + gate evidence impossible. Per the p4-apple README ("Allowed files scoped to
  apps/apple/**") the surface ships at the REAL convention: `TeslaSync/feature-views/VehicleAccessPage.*`.
  No `VehicleAccess*` stem pre-exists (no collision; clean `git add`).

